# The keys HELP's welcome text lists under "Main Screen": MainV2.ProcessCmdKey's F2 FlightData,
# F3 FlightPlanner, F4 Tuning, F5 "Refresh full param list", Control-F "Temp screen" and Control-T
# "Blind connect" (MainV2.cs:4087-4118, 4168-4180; crates/mp-gui/src/cmd_keys.rs).
#
# The claim: from HELP, F3 shows FLIGHT PLAN (MenuFlightPlanner_Click), F4 CONFIG
# (MenuTuning_Click: CONFIG/TUNING), F2 FLIGHT DATA (MenuFlightData_Click), and Control-F the
# EXPERIMENTAL tab (the owner's ruling of 2026-10-04 for `new temp().Show()`). F5 runs
# `comPort.getParamList()` and shows the screen showing again (MyView.ShowScreen) - with no
# vehicle there is nothing to fetch, and no fetch starts. Control-T, `comPort.Open(false)` on the
# connect box's port, with none chosen says so on the status line, where the C# boxes what `Open`
# throws. The keys work from any screen: F2 again from HELP.
#
# No vehicle. Its own data directory, with a config.xml checked for updates today, so no startup
# check asks anything over the keys. Run from the repository root:
#   tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/keys-main.gui
#
# Not yet run: the budget is a guess, set by hand until a passing run records one.
env XDG_DATA_HOME $WORK
setup mkdir -p "$WORK/MissionPlannerRust" && printf '<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><Config><update_check>%s</update_check></Config>' "$(date +%-m/%-d/%Y)" > "$WORK/MissionPlannerRust/config.xml"
screen help
window 1600x1200
budget 8

expect screen help
key F3
expect screen plan
key F4
expect screen config
key F2
expect screen fly
key ctrl+f
expect screen experimental

# F5: the parameters fetched when there is a vehicle to fetch them from, and the screen again.
key F5
expect screen experimental
expect params.fetch none

# Control-T: no port chosen.
key ctrl+t
expect status choose a port first

# From HELP again.
click tab-help
expect screen help
key F2
expect screen fly
